  <item>
    <title>”大学生哪有不发疯的！“如何逃脱早起的魔咒?</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/655717338fb8b597a28e70af</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">655717338fb8b597a28e70af</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 17 Nov 2023 07:33:07 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>时隔三个星期我又回来啦！这一期我们来谈谈早起，我相信早起对于大家来说都是一件非常困难的事情，但任何困难的事情都会有解决方法。</span></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="585">09:45</a>：早起的秘诀《早起的奇迹》</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="633">10:33</a>:早起的好处</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="721">12:01</a>：防贪睡五步法</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1246">20:46</a>：人生拯救计划</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2948">49:08</a> &nbsp;：浓缩版的人生拯救计划</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><blockquote><span>你长期坚持的任何事情都会变成习惯，而习惯是一种强大的力量。</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>早起的奇迹并不意味着你早起一个小时，然后度过更加漫长、更加辛苦的一天。它不在于你起得更“早”，而是起得更“巧妙”。</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>五分钟防贪睡策略：</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>第一分钟：睡前进行积极的自我暗示</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>第二分钟：将闹钟放到自己够不着的地方</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>第三分钟：直接走到盥洗室刷牙</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>第四分钟：喝下满满一大杯水</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>第五分钟：穿上晨练服出门锻炼（或者起床后立刻洗澡）</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>自我肯定永远不会有最终的版本，它只会不断地被修改、优化。</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>作者：哈尔·埃尔罗德</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>BGM：直到清晨黄昏（sampie this）</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>在剪辑中有一些小小的问题，请大家多多包涵！</span></blockquote>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/lisGgYRGa9rGm4_MyHsmSVttCmmP.m4a" length="51674250" type="audio/mp4"/>
    <itunes:duration>00:53:12</itunes:duration>
    <itunes:image href="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FpNyCZiOmxf2hyym_zkJRDmPROEO.jpg"/>
    <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
